Hi Gang!

Been away a while ... work and all that, you know how it goes ...

Last summer or fall when I was reading here, someone suggested
that I write up how I build NetHack as a free-standing
Windows executable using MinGW and the Cygwin shell.

The deal is, you work in the Cygwin environment, using Unix-style
commands and tools, but the program file you're building is *not*
linked to the Cygwin DLL, and can be run on any Windows computer
without Cygwin installed.

Fortunately, that's now a lot easier than when I started doing it,
since MinGW is now packaged as part of Cygwin.

Here's the easy way, in the hope that this makes hacking NetHack
accessible to more people:

http://www.crawfords.de/nh-cygwin-mingw-howto/

Comments and corrections welcome!

